# Conventional commits

Every commit message uses [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/).

```
<type>: <summary>
```

The summary starts with a capital letter. It says why the change exists. Keep it to one line.

Use these types:

- `feat` for a user-facing change
- `fix` for a bug fix
- `chore` for tooling, config, or maintenance
- `refactor` for a behavior-neutral code change
- `docs` for documentation only
- `test` for tests only
- `ci` for GitHub Actions and other CI

```
feat: Sign in with email and password
chore: Add ESLint and Prettier so hard-coded text fails lint
fix: Start in English when language setup fails
```

Do not write a summary with no type. Do not use `Feat:` or `FEAT:`.
